# Python bytecode from running the models
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# TLC scratch state (run-all.sh writes it to /tmp, but a manual run may not)
states/
*.st
models/results/*.spthy

# Reviewer2's file, managed by them and not read here [author, 2026-10-02]
AGENTS.md

# Conformance and acceptance run output, gigabytes of it, kept beside the
# repository and never part of it — **and now actually beside it**
# [2026-10-27]: `conformance-review` and `runs` are symlinks into
# `../FuerosNet-output/`, so the comment above is true of where the bytes
# are and not only of where git looks. The patterns carry no trailing
# slash because a symlink is not a directory to git.
conformance-review

# Build marker written by the crate sweep
crates/sweep.timestamp

# Field-test runs: every run directory the bench script writes
# (crates/tools/field-run.sh), bundles from the phones included; a symlink
# into `../FuerosNet-output/runs`, so a `git clean -fdx` takes the link
# and leaves 3.7 GB of runs where they are
runs

# The resource-design thread has left this tree [author, 2026-10-27]: the
# application-layer documents are a repository of their own
# (`../FuerosNet-applications`, which `CLAUDE.md` points at), the reviews
# of this implementation are in `Robot/reviews/`, and the experiment data
# is beside the repository with the other output. Nothing of it is ignored
# here any more, because nothing of it is here.

# Anonymising sidenet research: contextual work outside the core FN project
/anonymizing-sidenet/
